url: "https://github.com/khanukov/erdos302"
abstract: >-
  Version 0.2.0-preprint is a preliminary, unrefereed corrected snapshot of
  two-sided partial progress on Erdős Problem 302. Using Della Pietra's
  structured Problem 301 construction, an odd-quarter padding lemma gives a
  qualitative lower improvement over density 5/8. The required external Lean
  development is pinned and kernel-checked but unrefereed. Independently, an
  exact certificate gives the upper bound 140803024/163562355; this upper result
  does not depend on the Della Pietra developments. The results are not
  independently verified or peer reviewed and do not solve Problem 302. The
  finite semantics, exact packing certificates, omission argument, and upper
  asymptotic endpoint are connected
  by an end-to-end Lean 4 development with no external certificate hypothesis
  and are cross-checked by exact dependency-free software. For the publication
  candidate, the cache-free workflow rebuilds all 80,181 committed
  project-local Lean modules from source, verifies the exact 160,362
  .olean/.ilean output inventory, replays the final declarations, reproduces
  the axiom allowlist, and independently reads back the aggregate artifact.
  The Lean kernel/toolchain, operating system and hardware, and Mathlib remain
  disclosed trusted boundaries. The
  lower theorem is Lean-checked through pinned
  external formal developments. AI systems assisted with search, code,
  formalization, and audits; the named author remains responsible for all
  claims. Software and verification material are MIT-licensed; the manuscript
  is CC BY 4.0 under the path-specific scope in LICENSE_SCOPE.md. Zenodo
  automatically archives the tagged source after the GitHub release; the
  complete verified release assets remain attached to the GitHub Release.
